"Before an app connects to a site, your Mac looks its name up. Those lookups normally travel unencrypted, so your internet provider and anyone on the Wi-Fi can read every name. Switched on, NetworkMonitor sends each lookup encrypted to the resolver you pick, over DNS over HTTPS, and gives the answer back unchanged. Names only your network knows, like the router's, still go to it. If the resolver doesn't answer, lookups go to your network as before, so names keep working. Apps that encrypt their own lookups, like Chrome with Secure DNS, aren't affected." = "应用连接到某个网站之前，你的 Mac 会先查询它的域名。这些域名查询通常不加密，因此你的互联网服务提供商以及同一 Wi-Fi 上的任何人都能看到每个域名。开启后，NetworkMonitor 会通过 DNS over HTTPS 将每次域名查询加密发送到你选择的解析服务器，并原样返回结果。只有你的网络才知道的名称（例如路由器的名称）仍会发送到你的网络。如果解析服务器没有响应，域名查询会像以前一样发送到你的网络，因此域名仍能正常解析。自行加密域名查询的应用（例如开启了安全 DNS 的 Chrome）不受影响。";
